2/10/2025 H COW:Passed
HB0324H2001/ADOPTED

Page 1-line 4 After "plans;" insert "authorizing human resource
officer positions;".
Page 3-after line 7 Insert the following and renumber as necessary:
"(c) The state officials shall be assisted by human resource officers.
The human resources officers authorized under this section shall be hired by a
committee comprised of the state officials or their designees and housed within
the office of the state auditor. The state auditor shall ensure that the human
resources and payroll activities necessary for each state official are conducted
promptly at their direction and in accordance with applicable state and federal
law. A human resource officer employed under this section shall keep all
matters within a state official's office confidential as required by policies
of the state official.".
Page 3-line 9 Delete "(c)" insert "(d)".
Page 3-after line 21 Delete the House Standing Committee amendment
(HB00324HS001/A) to this line and further amend as
follows:
"Section 3. From existing appropriations and from existing employee
positions authorized by the legislature, the state auditor shall transfer two
hundred thirty-six thousand seven hundred twenty dollars ($236,720.00) and two
(2) full-time legislatively authorized employee positions from the department
of administration and information to the state auditor's office on the effective
date of this act. This appropriation and these positions are for purposes of
hiring the human resource officers specified in W.S. 9-1-104(c), as created by
this act, for the four (4) state officials. It is the intent of the legislature
that this appropriation be doubled and included in the state auditor's standard
budget for the immediately succeeding fiscal biennium.". ANDREW
